==Latin==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ef/|lang=la}}, {{X-SAMPA|/ef/|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{head|la|noun|head=ef|{{l|en|indeclinable}}}}

# {{n-g|The name of the letter ''{{l|la|F}}''.}}

====Usage notes====
* Multiple Latin names for the letter {{term||F}}, {{term||f}} have been suggested. The most common is {{term||ef}} or a {{l|en|syllabic}} {{term||f}}, although there is some evidence which also supports, as names for the letter, {{term||fē}}, {{term||əf}}, {{term||fə}}, and even (in the fourth- or fifth-century first Antinoë papyrus, which gives Greek transliterations of the Latin names of the Roman alphabet’s letters) {{polytonic|ιφφε}}.

